The root cause is that CI and local machines resolve tool versions independently — without explicit pinning, you get whatever the package manager happens to install. Here's how to fix it:

## Solution 1: Flox (Recommended for this repo)

Flox ensures bit-for-bit identical environments by declaring exact versions in a manifest. Since you're in a Flox repository, this is the most integrated option.

**Setup:**

1. Create/update `flake.nix` in your project root to declare all build tools:

```nix
{
  description = "Build environment";
  inputs = {
    nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable";
    flake-utils.url = "github:numtide/flake-utils";
  };
  outputs = { self, nixpkgs, flake-utils }:
    flake-utils.lib.eachDefaultSystem (system:
      let pkgs = nixpkgs.legacyPackages.${system};
      in {
        devShells.default = pkgs.mkShell {
          buildInputs = [
            pkgs.python312
            pkgs.nodejs_20
            pkgs.go_1_21
            # ... whatever tools you need
          ];
        };
      }
    );
}
```

