# Setting up project-local, pinned CLI tools with Flox

This project (which is part of Flox itself) can define a reproducible development environment using a **`flake.nix`** file. Tools declared there are available only when you enter the Flox environment, at exact pinned versions, without touching your system PATH.

## Setup

**1. Create `flake.nix` in the project root:**

```nix
{
  description = "Project dev environment with jq, yq, and AWS CLI";

  inputs = {
    nixpkgs.url = "github:nixos/nixpkgs/nixos-unstable";
    flake-utils.url = "github:numtide/flake-utils";
  };

  outputs = { self, nixpkgs, flake-utils }:
    flake-utils.lib.eachDefaultSystem (system:
      let
        pkgs = nixpkgs.legacyPackages.${system};
      in
      {
        devShells.default = pkgs.mkShell {
          buildInputs = [
            # Pin versions by specifying the package source
            pkgs.jq                # Latest from nixpkgs (or pin a specific commit)
            pkgs.yq                # Latest from nixpkgs
            pkgs.awscli2           # AWS CLI v2
          ];
        };
      }
    );
}
```

